    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "16ef4790_8eddb4f0",
        "filename": "rialto/src/requests/ec_key.rs",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T13:47:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Given that it\u0027s the code here that both generates the key and signs it, why do we need to include the key type in the serialization?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "a12cc8976088cec5297adc0c92d3226f410b8db3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9fdb4bf_3e8ba71a",
        "filename": "rialto/src/requests/ec_key.rs",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T15:28:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you mean by \"signing\" it?\n\nThe private key generated here is encrypted and sent to rkpd. It\u0027ll be fetched later during the client VM attestation for signing.",
      "parentUuid": "16ef4790_8eddb4f0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "a12cc8976088cec5297adc0c92d3226f410b8db3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4cdb66b4_9a8da318",
        "filename": "rialto/src/requests/ec_key.rs",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-20T15:35:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry, we generate it, then later we sign with it. No other party can access it, nor substitute a different key.\n\nSo we know the one we get back is the one we generated, so we know its exact type.",
      "parentUuid": "c9fdb4bf_3e8ba71a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "a12cc8976088cec5297adc0c92d3226f410b8db3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5530bf22_5f912e7d",
        "filename": "rialto/src/requests/ec_key.rs",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-21T08:33:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e ... we generate it, then later we sign with it.\n\nRight. Considering that the private key is not immediately consumed but obtained at a later time, it would be more reliable to obtain the DER encoding along with other relevant information. So we can perform additional checks, such as ensuring that the private key corresponds to the public key covered in the certificate.",
      "parentUuid": "4cdb66b4_9a8da318",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "a12cc8976088cec5297adc0c92d3226f410b8db3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b9ac164_c58ff6c9",
        "filename": "rialto/src/requests/ec_key.rs",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-21T13:40:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So are we going to check that the key type is what we expect? How does that benefit us?\n\nIf we only support one key type, then we should just persist the key; if we store any extra information then we have to check it is as expected when we retrieved it.",
      "parentUuid": "5530bf22_5f912e7d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "a12cc8976088cec5297adc0c92d3226f410b8db3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "09be4c8b_dc474c55",
        "filename": "rialto/src/requests/ec_key.rs",
        "patchSetId": 15
      },
      "lineNbr": 87,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-09-21T15:00:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually the curve doesn\u0027t matter so much since we only support one curve. I mostly want to verify that the public key in the certificate corresponds to the one stored in the private key during client VM attestation. \nDuring the attestation process, we receive a certificate and an encrypted private key. After decrypting the private key, there may be a discrepancy between the private key and the public key. It\u0027s more reassuring if we can do a verification there.",
      "parentUuid": "6b9ac164_c58ff6c9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 85,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 87,
        "endChar": 63
      },
      "revId": "a12cc8976088cec5297adc0c92d3226f410b8db3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
